$DIR/test.p:88:47: each variant of packed union P needs its own case clause
    Each variant of a union has a name of its own, which is not _, followed by
    its payload type if it has one. Variants have no tags, and in a packed union
    each variant has its own case clause.
    (see "Unions" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.13)
    (run "pluto explain E2404" for a longer explanation)
